## Vercel Web Analytics Configuration

Successfully configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Next.js App Router project.

### Changes Made

**Modified:**
- `src/app/layout.tsx` - Added Vercel Analytics component to the root layout

### Implementation Details

1. **Package Installation**: The `@vercel/analytics` package (v1.6.1) was already installed in package.json, so no additional installation was needed.

2. **Analytics Integration**: 
   - Imported `Analytics` component from `@vercel/analytics/next`
   - Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag after the `<Providers>` wrapper and children
   - This placement ensures analytics tracking is active across all pages

3. **Project Structure**: The project uses Next.js App Router with `src/app/layout.tsx` as the root layout file.

### Verification

- Build completed successfully with no TypeScript errors
- Dependencies installed and lock file (bun.lock) updated
- All 70 routes generated successfully in production build
- No breaking changes introduced to existing functionality

### Notes

The Analytics component will automatically track page views and Web Vitals metrics when the application is deployed to Vercel. The component is designed to have zero impact on performance and only loads tracking scripts in production environments.
